## **Revised ScreenDiet: API-Realistic Digital Nutrition**

### **What the Screen Time API Actually Gives Us:**

| **Capability** | **Limitation** |
|----------------|----------------|
| `FamilyActivitySelection` | User must manually select apps; we get tokens only after selection |
| `DeviceActivityMonitor` | Knows WHEN apps are used, not HOW (no scroll detection, no interaction data) |
| `DeviceActivityEvent` | Triggers based on time thresholds only, not behavior |
| `DeviceActivityCenter` | Historical data: total time per app category only, no granular patterns |
| `ShieldConfiguration` | Static UI per app category, limited dynamic content |
| `ShieldActionHandler` | Two actions: `.close` (give up) or `.defer` (delay) |
| `ManagedSettings` | Block/unblock apps, no behavioral conditions |

**Critical gaps:**
- ❌ Cannot detect infinite scroll, tap patterns, or interaction types
- ❌ Cannot analyze content velocity or exit friction
- ❌ Cannot see if user is creating vs. consuming within an app
- ❌ Cannot access App Store metadata (category, description) programmatically
- ❌ Cannot classify apps without user selection first

